sections: INPUT, OUTPUT, COMMENTS, STAMPS!!
{
	!! FOOP-33 §4: 'True and 'False resolve as ordinary ancestral (sibling)
	!! lookups into system.foo -- composed as the implicit root ancestor of
	!! every program. Note the LEADING QUOTE is required: a bare True (no
	!! quote) can never match the null-characterized 'True (searchable_name
	!! comparison is unconditional -- see FOOP-33.md §3 "quote-bearing
	!! search").
	!! Phase 5.5 (sequencer renders named creations) is PUNTED to a future
	!! FOOP -- see FOOP-33.md Open Questions for the get_recent_name()
	!! design. Once implemented, t1/t2/f1 below are expected to render as
	!! 'True/'True/'False instead of the bare ⬤ shown today; this baseline
	!! will need re-promoting at that time, not before.
	t1 = 'True;
	t2 = 'True;
	f1 = 'False;
}
!!
{
  t1=⬤;
  t2=⬤;
  f1=⬤
}!!
